WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.733
The CIS Controls include Implementation Groups, often called IG1, IG2, and IG3.

00:00:04.733 --> 00:00:08.594
These groups help organizations prioritize activities based on risk, complexity,

00:00:08.594 --> 00:00:09.752
and available resources.

00:00:09.752 --> 00:00:12.069
Smaller organizations often begin with IG1,

00:00:12.069 --> 00:00:15.930
while larger or more complex environments may implement additional safeguards.

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:20.177
Implementation Groups recognize that organizations have different needs and maturity levels.

00:00:20.177 --> 00:00:24.810
A small team with limited resources may need a different starting point

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.512
than a large enterprise with complex systems.

00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:30.215
This structure helps make the controls practical.

00:00:30.215 --> 00:00:35.620
It gives organizations a way to sequence improvement without losing sight of long-term maturity.
